{0 sqlkit}

Write [.sql] files with sqlc-style annotations; sqlkit asks PostgreSQL for the
parameter and result types of each query and emits typed OCaml.

{1 Packages}

- [sqlkit] — the runtime that generated code depends on. See {!module:Sqlkit}.
- [sqlkit-postgresql] — the [sqlkit] command and a libpq driver, [Sqlkit_pg].
- [sqlkit-caqti] — a Caqti/Eio driver with pooling, [Sqlkit_caqti].

{1 Entry points}

- {!module:Sqlkit} — [fetch_one], [fetch_all], [exec], [transaction].
- {!module:Sqlkit.Row} — decoders used by generated code.
- {!module:Sqlkit.Value} — encoders used by generated code.
- {!module:Sqlkit.Query} — the shape of a generated query module.
